[=#tdsversion]
= TDS Version =

The //tdsversion// option sets the TDS protocol version that SQL Relay uses with clients.  By default, it's chosen from the back-end database's version (eg. TDS 7.4 for SQL Server 2012 and later), or, if the back-end isn't one it recognizes, from the version the client asks for.  Valid values are 420, 500, 700, 710, 711, 720, 730, 731 and 740, for TDS 4.2 through 7.4.  Leaving it out, or setting it to 0, means auto-detect.  Some clients (eg. !FreeTDS) only negotiate encryption with TDS 7.1 or later, so if encryption isn't being negotiated, set it to 710 or higher.  See [tdsprototls.html TLS/SSL Encryption and Authentication].

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@parts/sqlrelay-tdsfeversion.conf@
}}}
